Package: snitch
Version: (injected by the deb assembly)
Installed-Size: (injected by the deb assembly)
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Marius Ciepluch <wishinet@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/norandom/snitch
Section: net
Priority: optional
Recommends: bpftool, default-dbus-session-bus | dbus-session-bus
Suggests: plasma-workspace, breeze-icon-theme
Description: egress control for Linux, decided at connect() in the kernel
 snitchd gates outgoing connections in the kernel (BPF LSM), keyed by the
 program's executable and the destination. Rules from /etc/snitch/rules.toml
 name who may talk to where; monitor mode reports, a bounded trial can enforce
 deny-by-default with a boot revert. The snitch tray binary shows connections
 and asks about the ones nobody has decided on yet. This package ships the
 daemon, the tray, their systemd units, the autostart desktop entry, a GRUB
 drop-in and a documented sample configuration as declared conffiles. The
 binaries are static (CGO_ENABLED=0), so the package declares no Depends:
 installation needs nothing but the archive. On GRUB hosts the package
 configures the next boot for the bpf LSM and runs update-grub; the systemd
 units and the desktop entry stay unpacked, never enabled. Recommended:
 bpftool, for the kill switch from a root console, and a D-Bus session bus,
 for the tray. Suggested: Plasma, whose panel hosts the tray, and the Breeze
 icons its notifications name.
